⚠️ **IMPORTANT: vendored copy of the credentials script has no drift guard**

`setup/install-source-git-credentials.sh` is byte-identical today to the reviewed `agents/setup/install-source-git-credentials.sh` (verified with `diff`), but it is a **third independent copy** (root `setup/`, submodule `agents/setup/`, factory checkout `factory-agents/setup/`) and only the submodule copy is pinned by `test/machine_kit/source_git_credentials_test.dart`. The header itself documents the failure mode: the inline copies "drifted / had to be fixed 6x" — that is exactly the gh-63 regression class. When the factory copy next gets a security fix (it has 14 review threads' worth of them), this root copy silently diverges.

Suggested guard (repo-idiomatic, cheap): assert byte-equality in the contract tests, e.g. in `source_git_credentials_test.dart`:

```dart
test('root setup/ copy stays in lockstep with the agents/setup copy', () {
  expect(
    File('setup/install-source-git-credentials.sh').readAsStringSync(),
    File('agents/setup/install-source-git-credentials.sh').readAsStringSync(),
    reason: 'two live copies of the credential installer must move in '
        'lockstep — a factory-side fix that misses the vendored copy '
        're-opens the gh-63 drift class',
  );
});
```

(or parametrize the existing `_scriptPath` groups over both files so the root copy inherits all 14 invariants).

⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the 5th reusable-workflow stub is not covered by the stub-ref guards**

This repo's convention is that every `IstiN/dmtools-agentic-workflows` stub is guarded by `test/machine_kit/factory_stub_ref_test.dart` ("The guards keep the stubs on immutable SHAs") — `machine-sm.yml`, `machine-merge.yml`, `merge-trigger.yml` and `ai-teammate.yml` are all covered, but this new `sm-kicker.yml` stub is referenced by no test (verified: `grep -rn kicker test/` is empty). Nothing prevents a future edit from moving this `uses:` to a branch ref, which — per the test file's own docstring — "executes whatever sits at the branch head" **with this workflow's `actions: write` permission**.

The pin itself is correct (full 40-hex SHA, verified: `factory-sm-kicker.yml` exists at `f0fe78c6…` and declares exactly the four inputs passed here, no required secrets, and its own `concurrency: factory-sm-kicker` group — so the stub correctly declares no caller-side concurrency, matching the machine-sm.yml constraint). It just isn't *enforced*. Add a guard with its own pin constant (own pin is right — the kicker intentionally pins a different commit than `_agenticWorkflowsPin`, per 33046d3):

```dart
const _smKickerPin = 'f0fe78c6225b99ca350f8354af112db937699b61';

test('sm-kicker stub pins the factory kicker at an immutable SHA', () {
  final yml = File('.github/workflows/sm-kicker.yml').readAsStringSync();
  final match = _agenticUsesRe.firstMatch(yml);
  expect(match, isNotNull, reason: 'sm-kicker.yml must call dmtools-agentic-workflows');
  expect(match!.group(1), '.github/workflows/factory-sm-kicker.yml');
  expect(match.group(2), _smKickerPin);
});
```

Worth also pinning the `with:` contract (`required_contexts: 'static,gate,agents-gate'` already has a lockstep duty with `test/release_required_checks_test.dart`).

